Subject: [PATCH] Phase B 6th corrective (C8/code): validate moved claim
 generation at dispatch entry, no fabricated attempt (PB-010 residual)

Sixth corrective on phase-b-source-index-architecture-completion, base
6adb9fac (E7); preserves all seven prior commits (80b4d13d, e488136f,
0464e347, 5aeb7ab3/C4, 8003ca02/E5, 3f4a9b2b/C6, 6adb9fac/E7) -- no amend.
Evidence lands in a separate evidence-only commit (E9).

Residual PB-010 defect: the moved dispatch branch computed
`expected_attempt = int(event.get("attempts") or 1)` BEFORE the direct
moved_invalid / unconfigured_root / _apply_moved_event terminalizations, so a
missing/None/0 generation was coerced to attempt 1. If the DB row was genuinely
at attempt 1, a direct guarded completion could succeed under a fabricated
generation -- contradicting the invariant (no default, no coercion, invalid
generation -> no queue mutation). C6 only hardened the last-resort backstop.

Fix (source_indexer.py; two edits, one module):
- Validate the claim generation at the moved DISPATCH ENTRY, before
  normalization, root lookup, dispatch, or any terminalization. No default, no
  coercion: type(x) is not int rejects bool/str; < 1 rejects 0/negative. An
  invalid generation performs NO queue mutation (continue -> leave 'processing'
  for requeue_stuck). Remove the `or 1` fallback.
- Extract the C6 generic-handler backstop into `_terminalize_moved_exception`
  (an independent last-resort boundary) so it stays directly testable; the
  drain delegates to it. Its own generation check remains as defense in depth.
  The terminalization exception is bound separately and only safe identifiers
  are logged (event_id, validated attempt, exception classes).

Tests (tests/test_source_index_moved_drain.py): the 3x7 matrix -- every invalid
generation (missing/None/0/negative/nonnumeric string/True/False) x every
dispatch class (valid_configured / moved_invalid / unconfigured_root) --
asserts _apply_moved_event, complete_owned_event and complete_event are all
uncalled, the FULL event row (status/attempts/error_code/updated_at/
next_attempt_at) is byte-identical to the post-claim snapshot, source/lineage/
destination content are untouched, and deterministic requeue_stuck recovers.
A direct `_terminalize_moved_exception` test covers the seven invalid forms plus
a valid generation whose guarded completion raises (swallowed) or succeeds. The
superseded backstop-only invalid-generation test is removed. Full moved-drain
suite green; ruff + mypy clean on the module.

No push / PR / deploy / prod DB / watcher activation / prod migration.

